---
title: High Protein Honey Garlic Chicken Fried Rice
servings: 4
tags: high-protein, batch, chicken, rice
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/sew6BNhyuRc/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://www.youtube.com/shorts/sew6BNhyuRc
time: 25 minutes
---

Start by grabbing your diced @chicken breast{600%g} in a #bowl{}, add @onion powder{1.5%tsp}, @garlic powder{1.5%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, and @soy sauce{35%ml}, then mix it and set it aside.

To make the best fried rice, to a #frying pan{} on high heat add @frozen mixed vegetables{300%g} followed by @egg{2} and @egg white{150%g}. Let it cook through and mix it together, then add the white part of the @spring onion{30%g} only, followed by day-old @cooked white rice{560%g}. Now add @&soy sauce{35%ml}, mix it together, then take it off the heat and add the green part of the @&spring onion{15%g} followed by @sesame oil{10%ml} and mix it all together one more time.

For the sauce, in a #bowl{} add @honey{65%g}, @&soy sauce{50%ml}, diced @garlic clove{8}, @reduced sugar ketchup{50%g}, and @rice wine vinegar{20%ml}, and mix it all together.

Cook the chicken in a #frying pan{} on medium to high heat for ~{4%minutes} each side. Once it's cooked, add the sauce followed by @cornflour{1%tsp} mixed with @water{80%ml} to help it thicken. Lower the heat and let it simmer on low heat for ~{5%minutes}, then equally divide the honey garlic chicken with the fried rice into four servings and enjoy.
